    {
        "content": "<p>Do you have a real world example where it makes a difference and where the current definition is not appropriate, or is it for the sake of doing the right thing?</p>",
        "id": 606011090,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1782222986
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmm, wouldn't it be one less assumption to keep track of when it is the comap algebra? But perhaps it's not worth the change</p>",
        "id": 606028239,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1782227042
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have seen this being used to construct the example of a system that has no natural invertible extension, but my motivation would be to just get rid of the assumption</p>",
        "id": 606030624,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1782227567
    }
]